@startuml
title UC-12 - Environment store selection and immutable revisions
autonumber
actor Developer as Dev
boundary SettingsUI as UI
control ConfigurationService as Config
database UnitOfWork as DB
participant OldStore as Old
participant NewStore as New
Dev -> UI: Save variable/secret(version)
UI -> Config: Scoped key validation and no active operation
alt ordinary Variable
 Config -> DB: New revision with ordinary value
else Secret
 Config -> New: Write immutable value to selected scoped store
 New --> Config: Opaque store-owned ref
 Config -> DB: CAS desired revision with ref only
end
Dev -> UI: Rename key, explicit update references checkbox
UI -> Config: Rename(newName, config/env/draft versions, opt-in)
Config -> DB: Read consistent desired/current metadata snapshot
opt update references selected
 Config -> Config: Lossless reconstruct missing drafts + exact KEY rewrite\n(preserve aliases, skip pending deletes)
end
Config -> DB: Atomic CAS config revision + all changed drafts\n(no active operation; current set unchanged)
DB --> UI: Safe pending configuration metadata
UI --> Dev: Explicit Preview then Deploy required
Dev -> UI: Change selected store(env/config versions)
UI -> Config: Claim scoped Environment operation
Config -> DB: Atomic version validation + owner claim
loop every desired Secret
 Config -> Old: Read original owning-store ref privately
 Config -> New: Copy immutable value and verify
end
Config -> DB: Atomic new desired revision + store selection, release owner
DB --> Dev: Pending consumer rollout, safe metadata
note over Old,New
Old applied refs/bundles remain valid.
Failure keeps old selection and cleans attempt-owned objects only.
No Secret bytes in UI/DB/logs.
end note
@enduml
